  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 5-10 EUR when the true market is in a downtrend (e.g., post-peak decline from 85+ to 70s), failing to capture the magnitude of the drop.",
    "Apply aggressive mean reversion after sentiment spikes: When sentiment history shows high values (1.00) followed by a sharp price peak, the model fails to anticipate the subsequent crash; forecasts should be reduced by 3-5 EUR immediately following such peaks.",
    "Adjust for lag in volatility: The model exhibits excessive inertia, smoothing out sharp price drops (e.g., 85.66 to 75.36) into a gradual decline; forecasts must be accelerated downward when the 3-day rolling average of true prices falls below the forecast.",
    "Invert sentiment correlation in bear markets: High sentiment scores (1.00) in the history often precede price collapses in this dataset; treat high sentiment as a contrarian sell signal rather than a bullish indicator.",
    "Horizon-specific correction: The model's 30-day forecast is too stable; apply a decaying adjustment factor that increases the downward slope of the forecast as the horizon extends beyond 10 days during periods of falling prices."
  ]
}
